========================================================================================================
  TARGET PRUNING — a target below the floor cannot be reached by any arm at any budget
  in the cap, because the floor already assumes the optimum was visited.
========================================================================================================
  A target is KEPT if some (cell, rule) can reach it. Dropping a target that
  only sigma=0.10 can reach would delete the noise contrast of §3.4, which is
  the headline of the experiment — 'reachable if you halve your assay CV' is
  the finding, not a nuisance. Targets unreachable everywhere measure only
  the cap, and those are the ones that go.

